WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Great job so far!

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.120
You've done a comprehensive analysis of the attributes in our

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.280
dataset and generated many interesting insights for the HealthStat team.

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:18.400
In this chapter, we will focus our efforts on putting the key elements together into a cohesive dashboard.

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:24.480
We will finish things off by optimizing the design and adding report navigation features.

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.720
Throughout this case study, our focus has been on measuring efficiency in hospitals,

7
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:34.680
which, as we discussed previously, is one of the six dimensions in healthcare quality.

8
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:42.400
We started with analyzing average LOS days and then added in the calculation of average cost per discharge.

9
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.880
Hospital management continually strives to reduce LOS and costs where possible

10
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:54.240
so as to maximize efficiency while not compromising the quality of patient care.

11
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.440
These are the insight themes we will be focusing on for the final dashboard product.

12
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:06.320
In our quest to analyze efficiency in hospitals across New York State, we found the average cost per discharge

13
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:15.720
for a hip replacement surgery was $21K, and that there was significant variability between hospital facilities.

14
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:24.400
Our root cause analysis found that some attributes stood out over others to influence both cost and average LOS.

15
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.640
Patients who had an extreme illness severity, and extreme or major

16
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:35.040
mortality risk stood out as having the most significant impact on reduced efficiency.

17
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.280
Also, hospitals located in New York City tended to have a higher cost and LOS

18
00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:48.000
overall, and lastly, that LOS was influenced by patient disposition to a skilled nursing home.

19
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.720
These insights are very useful and will help HealthStat to inform improvement initiatives for their clients.

20
00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:03.520
In this final chapter, we will work on building a report that provides concise insight to our stakeholders.

21
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:10.360
We will produce a clean, branded design that showcases the most important insights uncovered.

22
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:15.120
Here is a preview of some of the report components and contents.

23
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.480
Let's get back to it!

